    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=d70f3e50-2f3e-42b2-34f2-de1e9e667000": {
      "title": "Senior HR Business Partner",
      "description": "Department: Office VP of  Human Resources\nPosted: 2026-10-27\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Senior Human Resources Business Partner (SHRBP) serves as a trusted advisor and strategic partner to university leaders, managers, and employees on a broad range of human resources matters, with primary responsibility for employee relations and labor relations. The SHRBP provides timely, practical, and consistent guidance regarding employee performance, workplace concerns, conflict resolution, corrective action, policy interpretation, organizational change, and compliance with applicable employment laws and collective bargaining agreements. Working collaboratively with internal colleagues, the SHRBP promotes effective employee-management relationships, supports a positive and respectful workplace culture, and helps ensure that employment decisions and practices are fair, consistent, well-documented, and aligned with university policies and priorities. This role will also support labor relations activities, including contract interpretation and administration, grievance handling, preparation for labor-management meetings, and collective bargaining. You will: Serve as a primary HR advisor to leaders and employees on employee and labor relations, including performance management, coaching, corrective action, disciplinary matters, workplace conflict, and employee concerns. Conduct and support workplace investigations, including interviews, document review, fact assessment, and preparation of findings and recommendations. Advise on employee separations and workforce changes, including involuntary terminations, position eliminations, reorganizations, and restructuring. Review employment and disciplinary actions for consistency with University policies, collective bargaining agreements, applicable laws, and established practices. Administer and interpret collective bargaining agreements and participate in grievance administration, disciplinary proceedings, arbitration preparation, labor-management matters, and contract negotiations. Develop effective working relationships with union representatives and leaders. Partner with leaders to identify employee and organizational challenges, assess employee-relations implications, and develop practical HR solutions. Interpret and administer HR policies and assist with the development and revision of policies and procedures. Provide guidance on applicable federal and state employment laws, including FMLA, ADA, FLSA, paid leave, and anti-discrimination and anti-retaliation requirements. Identify emerging employee and labor relations issues and recommend appropriate strategies to HR leadership. You need: Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Labor Relations, Business Administration, Organizational Leadership, or related field required; graduate degree preferred. Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible HR experience, with demonstrated employee and labor relations experience; higher education experience preferred. Experience advising managers on performance management, corrective action, workplace conflict, employee complaints, and sensitive employment matters. Demonstrated experience conducting or supporting workplace investigations required. Experience with collective bargaining agreements, grievances, labor-management matters, and/or arbitration preparation required. Strong knowledge of employee and labor relations practices and applicable federal and state employment laws, preferably including Connecticut employment practices. Strong consultation, conflict-resolution, analytical, interpersonal, and written communication skills. Ability to interpret policies and collective bargaining agreements and translate requirements into practical guidance for managers, including providing appropriate training when required. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple complex and confidential matters with sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism. Ability to effectively balance employee concerns, management needs, institutional priorities, contractual obligations, and legal requirements. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable; *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. *Note - the budgeted salary for this position is $85,000"
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=60be9be1-ef76-ce57-c72e-dec11a58c089": {
      "title": "Director of Payroll and Student Employment",
      "description": "Department: Business Office\nPosted: 2026-10-23\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Director of Payroll & Student Employment serves as the primary manager for the Payroll and Student Employment Offices. This position is responsible for and accountable for directing the in-house payroll function and the time management systems for the University. This position will direct and participate in the preparation of the weekly and semi-monthly payrolls for faculty, staff, and students, ensuring compliance with all Federal and State laws as well as compliance with Union Bargaining Agreements. This role is also responsible for providing direction and support for the Student Employment Office (SEO) aimed at making the employment process for students and the University community as effective and efficient as possible. You will: Provides direction of all payroll related activities, including the supervision of administrative staff members. Provides direction of Student Employment Office (SEO) including the supervision of administrative staff members. Responsible for development, maintenance and compliance of payroll and SEO policies and procedures. Provides strategic leadership for Payroll operations while measuring and monitoring the effectiveness and efficiencies of the services provided. Ensures accurate and timely in-house processing of the University’s payrolls, weekly and semi-monthly, through Ellucian’s Banner system, time management systems, and payroll reporting requirements. Prepares and submits all federal and multi-state payroll tax reports, including quarterly and year-end returns; reviews non-wage payments for tax liabilities and acts as the general resource person for technical payroll and tax matters. Advises departments on payroll and taxation issues, policies, and procedures. Works with other members in the Business Office so the timely posting of all payroll transactions are properly recorded to the general ledger including reconciliations of payroll tax accounts and 403b liabilities. Manages tax table updates, W-2 processing, and develops the University’s annual payroll calendar. Assists with required data for various audits; financial statement, A-133, 403B and worker’s compensation. Reviews and recommends changes to improve operational effectiveness. Fosters an environment where a high level of customer service is delivered to faculty, staff and students. Understands and champions system changes, upgrades, and government mandated changes to payroll. Assists IT and HR in managing the implementation and maintenance of payroll and payroll related systems. Performs other duties as assigned You need: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Human Resources or related field, and a minimum of eight (8) years of experience in a senior level payroll manager position. Five (5) years of supervisory experience, preferably in payroll. Expertise in the end-to-end payroll process and a high level of understanding of general business operations and internal control concepts. Solid knowledge of federal and multi-state regulations and payroll fundamentals including payroll tax, reporting, balancing, pay policies, garnishments, and payroll best practices Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills are essential as are strong analytical, diagnostic, and problem-solving skills with attention to detail. A high level of technical skills and proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite. Ability to collaborate and communicate effectively across a wide range of constituencies. Ability to maintain and safeguard confidential and proprietary information. Preferred Qualifications: An MBA and prior work experience in a higher education environment. Experience with Ellucian’s Banner HR / Payroll system and TimeClock Plus time and attendance system preferred. Certified Payroll Professional (CPP) designation preferred. Whats in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave. *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. *Note - the budgeted salary for this position is $95,000 - 120,000"
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=e14b13ad-768a-833a-26ff-72b62467db61": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Department: Buildings & Grounds Maintenance\nPosted: 2026-10-21\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Custodian performs custodial duties, minor maintenance and other miscellaneous duties necessary to maintain the cleanliness, orderliness, appearance, sanitation and safety of university buildings and facilities both inside and outside. Work involves varied cleaning tasks, some of which may require heavy lifting. Assigned areas may include offices, classrooms, laboratories, residence halls rooms, meeting rooms, lounge areas, art gallery, auditorium, gymnasium, fitness center, and all corridors, hallways, and stairwells. Must be able to perform physical activities and work under inclement weather conditions. ESSENTIAL PERSONNEL :  This position is considered essential and requires the incumbent to report to work when the University suspends normal operations and classes and during inclement weather. You will: Clean, care and maintain buildings and facilities up to the standards and requirements set by the University of New Haven. Performs routine and comprehensive custodial maintenance of assigned facilities including, but not limited to: Vacuum, Sweep, Wet mop, Dust, Wax/Polish, Carpet care, Spot Removal, Window Cleaning, Rest Room Cleaning, Trash Removal, Recycling Removal, Litter Removal Cleans & disinfects restrooms, locker rooms, health centers, and other facilities and restock with adequate supplies. Use of all custodial equipment, materials and supplies in a safe and responsible manor to accomplish routine and comprehensive custodial operations. Strip, clean, buff and apply floor sealer and floor finisher to various types of hard floor surfaces using proper chemicals, supplies, equipment, and required safety gear in a safe and responsible manner. Spot clean and/or shampoo rugs, carpets, and furniture using proper chemicals, supplies, equipment, and required safety gear in a safe and responsible manner. Wash/clean accessible, interior and exterior windows, blinds, vents and screens which may require the use of ladders. Collects and properly disposes of recycling materials, empties bins and collection containers into proper recycling facilities. Maintains walks, common areas, entryways and areas surrounding assigned building by emptying trash, picking up litter, emptying cigarette butt containers, removing gum from and sweep and wash concrete areas as needed. Maintain storage areas and cleaning equipment, materials and supplies in a clean, safe and orderly manner. Communicates and documents all, facility repairs, equipment repairs, daily work status and work orders to supervisor. Observes safety standards and practices and reports all safety hazards to supervisor. Move furniture to prepare for cleaning, and event set-up and breakdown as needed. Work scheduled overtime, special events and be on call for emergencies. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to perform strenuous activities, including but not limited to walking, bending, standing, stooping, climbing stairs and ladders. Incumbent must also be able to lift and/or move items up to 60 pounds. You need: High School Degree or GED Three (3) years of custodial experience Knowledge of standard cleaning procedures, chemicals, products and equipment Must be able to drive and hold a valid CT state driver’s license. Must be able to use all necessary tools and equipment in a safe and proper manner. Perform duties in adherence to training standards and supervisory directives. Effectively communicate in English both oral and written. Ability to read and understand Safety Data Sheets, instructions, manuals, signs, posters and product label. Must be able to maintain acceptable work habits including but not limited to punctuality and regular and reliable attendance. Must work effectively with people from a variety of culturally diverse backgrounds. Must be able to work independently and in a collaborative manner with peers. Must have superior customer service skills and ability to respond in a professional, courteous, timely and effective manner to internal and external customers. Must maintain a neat, clean professional appearance. Must maintain a neat and clean work area. Disclaimer : The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the essential functions that will be required of the position. Duties may vary from incumbent to incumbent in this job. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. *Note- the budgeted hourly rate for this position is $24.03"
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=acdc010b-2ab0-328b-968d-4a788c9f3a98": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Biology & Environmental Science",
      "description": "Department: Biology & Environmental Science\nPosted: 2026-10-13\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded on the Yale campus in 1920, is a private, coeducational university that has been recognized by The Princeton Review and U.S. News & World Report for academic excellence. Located between New York City and Boston in the shoreline city of West Haven, the University is a diverse and vibrant community of nearly 10,000 students from across the globe. Within its five colleges, students immerse themselves in a transformative, career-focused education across the liberal arts and sciences, fine arts, business, engineering, public safety and public service. More than 100 academic programs are offered, all grounded in a long-standing commitment to collaborative, interdisciplinary, project-based learning Adjunct instructors are hired locally or regionally to teach specific courses in which they have particular expertise. They normally teach no more than half of the full-time load. Adjunct instructors receive a letter of appointment for each semester in which they teach; they are paid on a per-course basis. No expectation of continuing employment is implied. You will: The Department of Biology and Environmental Science at the University of New Haven invites applications for adjunct professors to teach a variety of courses in our Department during the Spring 2027 semester, with a potential to extend into future semesters. Available courses include: General Biology lectures Microbiology lectures and labs Molecular Biology lectures and labs Biochemistry lecture and labs Genetics lectures Anatomy and Physiology lecture and labs Introduction to Environmental Science labs Environmental Geoscience Introduction to Marine Affairs Marine Coastal Resource Management Marine Botany lecture and lab Ecological Applications lecture and lab You need: A minimum of a master’s degree in Biology or related field is required, Ph.D. preferred. The ideal candidate will have some teaching experience at the college level and a commitment to student-centered teaching is required. Preference will be given to those with a record of teaching excellence at the university level. Familiarity with online teaching is a plus, but these courses will require an on-campus component from the successful applicant. Application process: Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. The following materials are required. A brief cover letter explaining teaching experience and philosophy, a CV, and the name and contact information for three references. Finalists may be asked to submit examples of their teaching excellence, including syllabi and student evaluations. The University of New Haven does not provide immigration sponsorship or work authorization assistance for this position. Candidates must possess valid work authorization at the time of application. The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer, and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. Note: Compensation for new adjunct faculty begins at $1,200 per credit hour and can increase based on your highest degree earned and prior teaching experience."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=fa34de87-eed9-484b-bdc2-ccd71be6a89f": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator, Office of Residential Life",
      "description": "Department: Office of Residential Life\nPosted: 2026-10-10\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Area Coordinator staff member is an integral team member in organizing and implementing living and learning programs within our residential communities. The candidate must have the desire to work with a diverse group of students, staff, faculty, University administrators and external constituencies including parents. The position must carry out the mission and philosophy of the University of New Haven and is responsible for supporting and contributing to a positive atmosphere that facilitates respect, inclusivity and collaboration. You are: A proven problem- solver with a strong attention to detail. Committed to assuming leadership in a diverse, high-energy environment requiring the ability to consistently manage multiple simultaneous priorities. You will: Oversee a residential community and supervise, train, and evaluate student Resident Assistants (RAs) Be a live-in presence for 350-450 residents within your assigned residential community, working day, weekend, evening hours and university holidays Supervise graduate level Residence Hall Director Design, implement and assess a residential programming strategy that supports retaining students at the University as well as in housing. Programs include mentoring, social and educational programs, orientation programs, summer camps and conferences Oversee the maintenance work order process as well as the damage billing process while working collaboratively with Facilities to address area needs and issues Coordinate operational aspects of residence hall openings and closings; health and safety inspection process, schedule fire drills and room inventory process for areas of supervision. Serve as a resource for students seeking support and a referral agent to other resources on campus regarding academic, personal, or mental-health concerns Conduct disciplinary counseling and hearings for violations of University rules and regulations. Engages in opportunities to increase own capacity for equity, diversity, and inclusion and encourages cultural competency among students Participate in departmental, divisional and institutional committees as assigned You need: A Bachelor’s degree (required); master’s degree preferred Two years of professional residential experience preferred. Proficiency with The Housing Director (THD) housing management software and Maxient conduct management software preferred. A valid Driver’s License What’s In It For You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. *Note - the budgeted salary for this position is $47,000."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=cac73c5e-c68b-f04b-254e-48e2753998e7": {
      "title": "Environmental Health & Safety Specialist",
      "description": "Department: Public Safety\nPosted: 2026-10-09\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Environmental Health and Safety Specialist assists the Public Safety and Administrative Services Department in maintaining a safe and healthy work and learning environment across all University campuses. This position helps design, develop, implement, and oversee programs that ensure regulatory compliance and promote policies and procedures that improve campus environmental health and occupational safety. In addition, the position assists with the development, planning, and execution of environmental health and safety training for faculty, staff, students, visitors, vendors, and construction workers when applicable. The position also investigates accidents, incidents, and near misses occurring on university properties, identifies root causes, and recommends corrective actions. You will: Oversee and administers the day-to-day operations of the Environmental Health and Safety program, ensuring compliance with University, State, and Federal policies and regulations. Serve as a liaison with university lab managers and as a resource for staff and other groups to identify, develop, and assist with implementing specific EHS programs, processes, and practices. Assist with conducting hazard assessments to prevent or reduce incidents related to environmental health and safety. Assist in accident, incident and near miss investigations and prepare reports outlining investigation results and corrective recommendations to the safety committee. Oversee Velocity Online chemical inventory/SDS database. Ensure proper storage, shipment, and management of hazardous, universal, and biological waste. Conduct and coordinate training to comply with university policy and regulatory requirements. Provide input in the design of laboratory systems and safety standards. Develop, revise, and publish University environmental health and safety policies. Assist Facilities with conducting inspections, testing, follow-up inspections, and reporting for Environmental Health and Safety systems to ensure compliance. Maintain documentation for all related environmental health and safety matters. You need: Master's degree (preferred) or Bachelor's Degree in Environmental Health & Safety, chemistry, biology, chemical engineering or related sciences RCRA, DOT, OSHA 40-hour training certifications required. CHMM certification preferred Current HAZWOPPER certification preferred Minimum 3 years of experience in academic or research laboratory environment. Experience working with a university-based population preferred Must have valid driver’s license and any pass pre-employment checks required by Human Resources Ability to effectively use Microsoft Office application suite and applicable applications Strong data management skills Must be able to communicate effectively with a diverse campus population Public speaking and group presentation experience desired Experience working and applying principles and accepted practices of laboratory safety at a university or similar setting Knowledge of chemical, biological and radiological handling, storage and safety procedures Experience with the selection and use of industrial hygiene, chemical and radiation monitoring equipment for the effective evaluation of associated laboratory hazards Familiarity with the selection and appropriate use of personal protective equipment for managing personal safety Ability to interpret, implement and comply with federal, state and local regulations and interact with agencies Skilled in developing clear and concise technical reports and training materials Excellent written, verbal and analytical skills and strong attention to detail Demonstrated outstanding interpersonal skills Willingness to work collaboratively in support of all areas of the Public Safety Department Excellent organization and time management skills Must be medically fit and able to wear respiratory protection What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. Note: The hiring range for this position is from $63,000-$82,000."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=95ca88db-13d5-b51d-cc73-b979bcb33870": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Sociology",
      "description": "Department: Psychology\nPosted: 2026-10-06\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . Adjunct instructors are hired locally or regionally to teach specific courses in which they have particular expertise. They normally teach no more than half of the full-time load. Adjunct instructors receive a letter of appointment for each semester in which they teach; they are paid on a per-course basis. No expectation of continuing employment is implied. The University of New Haven is searching for adjunct instructors in Sociology to begin in Spring 2027. The position supports the instructional needs of the Psychology and Sociology Department in teaching. You will: Teach one or more courses in undergraduate sociology, including Introduction to Sociology You need: At least a master's degree or Ph.D. in Sociology or a related disciple (e.g. Social Work) At least one year of experience teaching college-level preferred Excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to prepare courses with best pedagogical practice in mind Experience with instructional technology Familiarity with, or the ability to quickly adopt, the Canvas LMS. Application Process Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The following materials are required: A brief cover letter explaining teaching experience and a CV including a list of courses previously taught. *The University of New Haven does not provide immigration sponsorship or work authorization assistance for this position. Candidates must possess valid 