    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=d76859d0-2df2-30e6-e7be-d3f5537e6e30": {
      "title": "Junior-Level Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program",
      "description": "Department: Allied Health \nPosted: 2026-09-24\nClinical Assistant Professor Junior-Level Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program Department of Allied Health Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Dental Hygiene Program, based in the Department of Allied Health in the School of Health Sciences at the University of New Haven is seeking to hire a full-time Non-Tenure Track Faculty. This faculty member will teach in the Associate in Science and Bachelor of Science Dental Hygiene Programs and supervise junior-level clinical experiences according to the accreditation standards established by ADA CODA. The successful candidate will be committed to academic and scholarly excellence, continuous improvement through professional development, and self-assessment. This position is to begin Spring 2027. The University of New Haven’s School of Health Sciences (SHS) is one of the most progressive health sciences schools in the United States for its approach to integrating all health professionals – from technicians to physicians – in an interdisciplinary, interprofessional educational experience focused on public health, ethics, and health technology. Students develop the competencies necessary to be a successful healthcare professional in the 21st century through hands-on experiences and a curriculum focused on healthcare innovation, systems thinking, and using evidence-based approaches to solve today’s biggest challenges in healthcare. The School of Health Sciences includes the Departments of Allied Health, Population Health and Leadership, and Rehabilitation Sciences and Wellness. You will: Teach in the Associate in Science and Bachelor of Science dental hygiene programs both didactic and clinical courses Communicate with and manage outside clinical sites, maintain and update site contacts, requirements and paperwork, prepare clinic rotation schedules, address student-related or instructor-related site issues Conduct instructor calibration meetings, orientation and training. Coordinate University of New Haven Dental Hygiene Center clinic rotations, ensure local, state and federal compliance, and maintain responsive communication with students and instructors. Serve on departmental, school, and university level committees Advise and support students Maintain currency in the Dental Hygiene discipline and teaching methodologies Maintain compliance with the American Dental Association Commission on Dental Accreditation and submits reports and data as needed Other duties as directed You need: Earned Master’s degree in Dental Hygiene or an appropriate terminal degree in their discipline Minimum 3 years of clinical teaching and 1 year of didactic teaching experience in a dental hygiene program Experience with clinical coordination preferred Current Connecticut dental hygiene license, eligibility for dental hygiene licensure in Connecticut, and certification in local anesthesia Knowledge of dental hygiene accreditation, technology common in dental hygiene practice and education, and computer applications commonly used in dental hygiene Employment is contingent upon successfully passing a background investigation and proof of Connecticut Dental Hygiene Licensure. Application Instructions: All information on candidates will be kept confidential. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. Qualified candidates should submit: 1) a cover letter describing their academic and/or industrial experiences relevant to the position, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and 4) contact information for at least three professional references (reference checks will not occur without permission). What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable Join an academic community of dedicated & supportive colleagues *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. Note: The budgeted salary for this position is $65,000. UNH is an Equal Opportunity Employer"
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=8861a5f1-8c69-d3ad-5ad0-af29cf9c88de": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "Department: Admissions\nPosted: 2026-09-04\nAssistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions - Enrollment Management Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . Reporting to the Director of Recruitment, the Assistant Director of Admissions will manage a travel territory, create a travel schedule, and attend college fairs and high school visits both in person and virtually representing the university. The individual will be responsible for application review and follow up efforts. In addition, work on-campus recruitment events and daily information sessions. You are: Committed to enrolling and retaining a diverse student body An excellent communicator and connector, with the ability to interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty and staff Customer-oriented and able to provide the best experience to all prospective students You will: Assist in the identification, recruitment, and enrollment of prospective students from a geographic territory Conduct enthusiastic on-campus, off-campus and virtual information sessions while working special recruitment events throughout the year Represent the University of New Haven at college fairs, college nights and virtual programs throughout the year Provide admission counseling to prospective students and be responsible for day-to-day communication with students in person, via telephone, zoom, text or email Be responsible for carrying out aspects of the admission and recruitment process including, but not limited to, planning and executing fall and spring recruitment travel Coordinate time-sensitive application workflow and process applications, including the evaluation of candidates for admissions, utilizing university guidelines to determine admissibility of students and ensuring that accepted students receive appropriate communication Counsel prospective students, parents and guidance professionals throughout the college application and selection process Perform other duties as assigned and necessary in order to meet the mission of the University and the school’s enrollment goals You need: A Bachelor's degree is required; Master’s Degree preferred The ability to represent the University of New Haven in a variety of situations and be able to competently interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty and staff Excellent interpersonal and written communication skills Excellent organizational, planning, and project management skills A high level of technical skills and proficiency in Microsoft suite of products required The ability to travel on behalf of the University representing the school at various recruitment events A valid driver's license The ability to lift up to 50 pounds is required for the travel component of the position The ability to work evening and weekends, as needed What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable"
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=b745fa6c-c2f5-4121-574e-4a2ab72f1a04": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Research Administration",
      "description": "Department: Office Provost/VP Academic Affairs\nPosted: 2026-09-02\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The University of New Haven is seeking an experienced, highly motivated, hands-on research administrator to lead the collegial and knowledgeable team in the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs and to support the University’s continued growth in areas of research and external funding. The position is responsible for leading the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs (OGSP), overseeing all aspects of proposal review and submission, facilitating negotiation of award terms and conditions, and identifying and resolving issues through the life-cycle of an award. The Executive Director will be responsible for responding to the needs of researchers, supporting research processes, infrastructure, and procedures, and working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and administrators to foster a positive, productive, and growing research environment. The Executive Director collaborates with the Office of the Provost, Deans, the Business Office, the Finance Director of Sponsored Programs and other leaders as well as external sponsors and agencies to ensure compliance with funder requirements and cooperation in the execution and management of sponsored programs/projects. The Executive Director will be responsible for collaborating with other research stakeholders on issues such as research agreements, fee-for-service contracts, material transfers, confidentiality/non-disclosure agreements, sub-award management, export controls, and FCOI. The position is responsible for maintaining knowledge of and responding to changes in federal government requirements, sponsor terms and conditions, and shifting levels of sponsor funding. The Executive Director will lead strategic planning and policy development for OGSP and will develop goals, objectives, and strategies and operational plans in accordance with the direction of the strategic plan. You will: Strategic Leadership & Administration Provide vision, direction, and operational management for the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs (OGSP), including supervision and professional development of all office staff. Develop and implement policies, procedures, and systems for the administration of sponsored programs consistent with federal regulations (2 CFR 200 Uniform Guidance), sponsor requirements, and institutional priorities. Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and academic department chairs to align sponsored programs strategy with institutional research goals and the University strategic plan. Oversee all aspects of proposal review and submission, negotiating award terms and conditions and resolving issues throughout the award life cycle. Serve as institutional liaison to federal agencies, private foundations, and corporate sponsors on matters of policy, compliance, and relationship management. Respond to researcher needs and support research processes, infrastructure, and procedures in collaboration with faculty, staff, and administrators. Oversee the OGSP operating budget, and report regularly to institutional leadership on research activity metrics. Lead the development and maintenance of the institution's F&A cost rate agreement in coordination with the cognizant federal agency and institutional finance leadership. Allocate staff workload to maximize OGSP effectiveness and ensure appropriate resource allocation. Implement Artificial Intelligence where appropriate in alignment with University initiatives. Perform other related duties as assigned. Compliance & Risk Management Serve as the institution's primary point of accountability for compliance with all federal, state, and sponsor regulations governing sponsored programs, including Uniform Guidance, agency-specific requirements, and research integrity standards. Serve as the institutional point of contact for export control policy and administration, ITAR registration, intellectual property requests, and technology transfer inquiries. Coordinate the institution's human subjects research administration in conjunction with the Chair of the IRB committee, ensuring Federalwide Assurance (FWA) compliance, protocol coordination with active awards, and appropriate training for research personnel. Manage institutional risk related to sponsored programs, including identification of compliance vulnerabilities, development of mitigation strategies, and coordination with internal audit and legal counsel as appropriate. Ensure timely and accurate institutional reporting to federal and other sponsors, including FFATA/FSRS subaward reporting, Single Audit preparation, and closeout documentation. Oversee export controls, conflict of interest disclosures, and responsible conduct of research (RCR) training in coordination with relevant institutional offices. Track, disseminate, and respond to changes in federal government requirements, sponsor terms and conditions, funding trends, and local, state, and federal regulations affecting sponsored programs administration. Faculty & Stakeholder Engagement Serve as primary advisor to principal investigators on sponsored programs matters, providing guidance on complex compliance issues, sponsor relationships, and research administration strategy. Collaborate with principal investigators on budget development and proposal submissions. Develop and deliver faculty training and outreach programs on sponsored programs policies, procedures, and funding opportunities. Partner with research stakeholders on research agreements, fee-for-service contracts, material transfer agreements, confidentiality/non-disclosure agreements, sub-award management, export controls, and financial conflict of interest (FCOI) matters. Establish and maintain clear protocols with the Office of Advancement for the handoff of private foundation awards and with the Office of Innovation for corporate awards carrying sponsored program obligations, ensuring appropriate administrative oversight. Collaborate with the Business Office and Finance Director of Sponsored Programs to ensure compliance and cooperation in the execution and management of sponsored programs. Represent the institution in professional organizations including NCURA (National Council of University Research Administrators) and relevant regional networks. Signatory Authority Serve as the institution's Authorized Organizational Representative (AOR) for all proposal submissions and award acceptances. Execute grant agreements, contracts, subaward agreements, memoranda of understanding, and other sponsored program instruments on behalf of the institution. Negotiate award terms and conditions with federal agencies, state agencies, and private sponsors to protect institutional interests while advancing the research mission. You need: Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree strongly preferred in research administration, public administration, business, or a related field. Minimum of 8 years of progressively responsible experience in sponsored programs or research administration in a higher education setting, including at least 3 years in a supervisory or leadership role. Significant experience in pre-award and non-financial post-award areas and an understanding of post-award financial management; Knowledge of compliance issues and implementation strategies; Ability to communicate effectively across a wide range of constituencies; Excellent time management skills and attention to detail The Executive Director must have a hands-on style working with faculty on budget development and proposal submissions and day-to-day tasks in this very busy five-person office. External funding support includes federal, state, other governmental agencies, foundations, non-profit community organizations, corporate contracts, and collaborative agreements with other institutions of higher education. Technical skills include Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), some knowledge of Banner or equivalent system, database such as Cayuse or DataWarehouse, and experience with sponsor portals including Research.Gov and Grants.Gov. Applications will be reviewed as they are received until the position is filled. For additional information contact Dr. Ronald Harichandran, Vice Provost for Research (rharichandran@newhaven.edu). Application materials must include: a cover letter, a resume/CV, and contact information for three professional references What's in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=0f6e51f0-eb17-b9f8-70f8-799543558251": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Department: One Stop Student FIn'l & Reg Svcs\nPosted: 2026-08-03\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Assistant Director of Financial Aid will contribute to the Office of Financial Aid by being part of a team that provides frontline customer support and service regarding financial aid. The assistant director will also review aid files, process aid awards, and support the operation of the Financial Aid Office and the One Stop Office. You will: Perform needs analysis, packaging and verification of student financial aid awards and files Process financial aid for all students studying away from UNH including study abroad, co-op programs, etc Counsel students and families regarding aid applications, eligibility and programs Assist with student and parent loan processing Generate financial aid reports as needed Present financial aid information and workshops both on and off campus to a variety of audiences Remain informed and updated on state and federal financial aid regulations Assist the Office of Financial Aid by providing exceptional service to students and other customers, both internal and external, in person, online, and via phone and email Propose innovative solutions to issues identified during customer contact Research process improvements and implement efficiencies Promote teamwork, collaboration, and resource sharing across the Office of Financial Aid and other Enrollment Services areas QUALIFICATIONS, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES: Administrative experience in higher education desired Bachelor’s degree preferred and two to four years of experience in a Financial Aid Office preferred – equivalent experience may be considered in lieu of a degree Experience with Banner preferred Experience with PowerFAIDS preferred Knowledge of Title IV financial aid regulations Understanding and comprehension of federal tax returns Excellent verbal and written communication skills and interpersonal skills are required A commitment to enhancing the internal and external customer experience is required Professional presentation and demeanor is required Proficiency with the Microsoft suite of products including, but not limited to, Word, Excel, Outlook and Teams is necessary Excellent organizational skills and great attention to detail with the ability to prioritize and advance multiple tasks simultaneously Ability to work independently and take individual initiative as well as the ability to work as a collaborative team member Ability to work early morning, evening, and/or weekend hours as needed in support of student events and initiatives Whats in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=c59e165e-1e54-d963-2f1e-636630cadd44": {
      "title": "Admissions Support Representative",
      "description": "Department: Admissions\nPosted: 2026-07-07\nAdmissions Support Representative Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded on the Yale campus in 1920, is a private, coeducational university that has been recognized by The Princeton Review and U.S. News & World Report for academic excellence. Located between New York City and Boston in the shoreline city of West Haven, the University is a diverse and vibrant community of nearly 9,000 students from across the globe. Within its five colleges, students immerse themselves in a transformative, career-focused education across the liberal arts and sciences, fine arts, business, engineering, public safety and public service. More than 100 academic programs are offered, all grounded in a long-standing commitment to collaborative, interdisciplinary, project-based learning The Admissions Support Representative is an integral member of the Office of Admissions, providing exceptional customer service while supporting the daily operations of the admissions office. As one of the first points of contact for prospective students, families, school counselors, and campus visitors, this position helps create a welcoming and engaging experience that reflects the University's commitment to student success. The Admissions Support Representative coordinates campus visit operations, supports recruitment initiatives, assists with the planning and execution of admissions events, and contributes to achieving the University's enrollment goals. You will: Serve as the primary front desk representative, welcoming campus visitors and ensuring a professional, friendly, and organized check-in experience for prospective students, families, school counselors, and guests. Manage the main admissions phone line, responding to inquiries with exceptional customer service and directing calls to the appropriate staff as needed. Communicate with prospective students, families, and school counselors via phone, email, text, and in person, providing timely, accurate, and personalized information about the admissions process and the University. Coordinate daily campus visit logistics, including confirming visit registrations, preparing visit materials, and ensuring prospective students and guests have a seamless and engaging campus experience. Collaborate with student ambassadors and campus tour guides to coordinate daily schedules, maintain adequate tour coverage, and support a high-quality visitor experience. Conduct on-campus information sessions for prospective students and families, effectively communicating admissions information, academic opportunities, and campus resources. Create, maintain, and manage daily admissions staff and visitor coverage schedules to ensure efficient front desk operations and successful campus visit programming. Assist with application review and processing during peak admissions periods, as needed. Assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of admissions recruitment events, including Open Houses, Explore Days, Accepted Student programs, counselor events, and other on- and off-campus recruitment initiatives. Support event logistics, registration, setup, execution, and post-event follow-up to ensure successful programs and a positive guest experience. Collaborate with admissions staff and campus partners to continuously enhance visitor experiences and improve admissions operations and event effectiveness. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission of the University and the achievement of institutional enrollment goals. You need: Bachelor's degree required; and a minimum of 1 year of admission experience preferred. Proven customer service skills and minimum of 1 year of experience. Ability to represent the University of New Haven in a variety of situations and be able to competently interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty, and staff. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and written communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft suite of products required; Slate CRM system experience preferred. Willingness to work evening and weekends when required. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds is required for the travel component of the position. Must demonstrate a tireless commitment to enrolling and retaining a diverse student body. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=c167cdc3-9f46-c777-73ed-a0e9e4d7c5be": {
      "title": "Facilities Manager Shift Operations (2nd Shift)",
      "description": "Department: Buildings & Grounds Maintenance\nPosted: 2026-05-29\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded on the Yale campus in 1920, is a private, coeducational university that has been recognized by The Princeton Review and U.S. News & World Report for academic excellence. Located between New York City and Boston in the shoreline city of West Haven, the University is a diverse and vibrant community of nearly 9,000 students from across the globe. Within its five colleges, students immerse themselves in a transformative, career-focused education across the liberal arts and sciences, fine arts, business, engineering, public safety and public service. More than 100 academic programs are offered, all grounded in a long-standing commitment to collaborative, interdisciplinary, project-based learning. The Facilities Manager Shift Operations has primary responsibility for Physical Plant operations during hours assign. This includes all shift staff and contractors, the site's HVAC and Utility systems and auxiliaries which require continuous monitoring, repair and preventative maintenance serving the academic, student life, athletic and administrative facilities. Working relationships with various personnel levels (bargaining level through management) associated with several hundred different HVAC and building utility systems which vary in importance, complexity and age are an integral part of this position. This position will act as shift watch stander with primary oversight of the campus building management systems. This position will respond directly or direct staff to off design conditions in all buildings. In addition, will monitor remotely and triage off design conditions campus wide and respond locally when necessary. The incumbent will be responsible to coordinate the day-to-day operation of the site's heating, ventilating and air conditioning (HVAC) systems, building management system(s), and associated auxiliary services and systems. Day to Day oversight and management of personnel assigned to the shift. Responsible to set priorities, coordinate with and dispatch operating personnel (Trade mechanic's & contractors) in facilities and systems operation and repairs. Identify, plan, and assist the facilities staff in the performance of scheduled and unscheduled maintenance of HVAC systems and associated auxiliary services and equipment. You will: Monitor Building Management System (Including remote locations) Respond independently to Off Design alarms and taking corrective or mitigating actions (remote location– dispatch appropriate support/service staff). Manages and may respond directly to Service calls (either from day time Facilities call line or directly during Off-hours) Monitoring Fire Alarms and manages responding as facilities representative taking corrective or mitigating actions as assigned Manages Work Order and Service Requests during off hours. Manages and directs “On Call” or Facilities shift staff as required Provides technical and engineering services, including know-how for building processes, equipment procurement, and equipment function in order to maintain efficient operation of facilities. Support of the groups and departments occupying the buildings and site facilities in the area of responsibility. Supporting facilities department trade/contract employees assigned in those areas to ensure the operability, reliability, efficiency and safety of plant and building systems and equipment. Will work in close collaboration with Facilities leadership and staff in support of ongoing 24/7 Operations. Maintain proper operation of site HVAC and Building systems. Interact with various department personnel to develop energy efficient HVAC operating schemes. Implement schemes developed. Give work direction and train maintenance personnel in correct maintenance procedures for HVAC systems (i.e., rebuilding of control valves, humidifiers, VAV boxes, etc.). Provide HVAC and building system expertise to facilities department with regard to renovations and new construction. Interact with Facilities Manager and Building occupants directly to provide problem solving expertise on specific HVAC and building systems related issues and problems. Manages operation of utility plant equipment and systems such as boilers, cooling towers, refrigeration, HVAC, electrical distribution, air compressors, waste water system, etc., in a safe and economical manner. Manages engineering logs and records Assist in major equipment repairs. Responsible for supervision and coordination with trade staff of all utility equipment shutdowns, startups, including lock-out/tag-out safety procedures. Provide assistance to Facilities Operations management in coordination of all electrical distribution changes. Insures all mechanical spaces are maintained in a clean and safe condition. Insures maintenance of proper boiler water, glycol, DI water, RO water, condenser water chemistry. This includes water testing and chemical treatment. Manages the response to temperature complaint calls from site's general population, assuring that people comfort and indoor air quality issues are properly addressed and resolved. Responsible for coordinating and implementing shutdowns for preventive maintenance and repair work in collaboration with the operating departments and building occupants. Responsible for developing and implementing an effective preventive maintenance program in conjunction with West Haven campus maintenance departments as well as end users, in order to maintain equipment, buildings and site facilities in optimal condition. Maintains records via the CMMS system. When acting as project leader, the Facilities Manager Shift Operation determines the resources needed to meet the project requirements regarding costs, timing, performance and quality. This includes staffing needs. As project leader, the Facilities Manager Shift Operation is responsible for supervising and coordinating the work of internal and external resources that are working on the project. Responsible to operate in a safe and efficient manner and area in compliance with all applicable rules and regulations, including OSHA, environmental, safety and security concerns. Is not relieved from an assigned shift till relief arrives (or supervisor releases) and Responsible for all physical plant condition upon assumption of shift duties The Facilities Manager Shift Operation is deemed an essential employee and therefore, must be able to report to work if the University suspends normal operations and classes due to inclement weather. You need: The Facilities Manager Shift Operation must be able to quickly assess and resolve problems associated with daily facilities operations and services. Must be able to read blueprints/drawings including piping, mechanical and electrical, The ability to work independently and in a collaborative manner with others. Ability to prioritize duties, with a strong focus on attention to detail and completing assignments and meeting deadlines. Ability to work overtime. A valid Connecticut Driver’s License A strong customer service orientation and ability to interact with a diverse constituency. Ability to speak, read and write English. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS This position requires strenuous physical activity, including but not limited to walking, bending, standing, stretching, climbing stairs and ladders, and the ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Disclaimer: The intent of this job description is to prove a representative summary of the essential functions that will be required of the position. Duties may vary from incumbent to incumbent. The hours for this position are Sunday-Wednesday, 4pm-2am. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment."
    },
    "https://apply.clearcompany.com/newhaven?jobId=acf8d7b5-a447-dee5-fe78-96f995e61f47": {
      "title": "Facilities Planning Manager",
      "description": "Department: Buildings & Grounds Maintenance\nPosted: 2026-04-07\nWho we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Facilities Planning Manager is responsible for management and administration of the university facilities planning for all campuses including but not limited to West Haven and others as assigned. Position has direct responsibility for the university’s Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS), Preventive and Reactive Work Order Control. Overall responsibility for development of written PM procedures. Operational oversight of business operations within Facilities Operations including purchase requisitions, processing of invoices for payment, procurement of parts/materials as needed and managing the 24/7 phone line for facilities. Position manages the hiring of and supervision of student office employees. Position must work with the various maintenance supervisors and other university leadership (Residential Life, Academic Affairs, Campus Safety, Business Office, Etc.) to develop strategies and programs consistent with the individual area needs (e.g. Res Life, Facilities, Business Office, Utilities, Athletics, Grounds, Etc.). Position has responsibility for maintaining facilities programs and records required for meeting all regulatory requirements including but not limited to OSHA, EPA, DEEP, IBC, and University’s Standards. Position is also responsible in association with site IT resources, for CMMS system hardware and software maintenance. You will: Manage site centralized Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS). Responsible for developing written preventative maintenance action for incorporation into system including assets associated with new construction or renovations. Assess all work requests to determine scope of work and provide required direction relative to materials, equipment, manpower, and time for execution of work to complete the job. Oversight of business operations for Facilities Operations including supervision of student clerical staff. Position ensures smooth flow of business activity consistent with University Standard Operation Procedures for purchase requisitioning, submissions of invoices for payment, recordkeeping and budget oversight with reporting responsibility to Director of Facilities Business & Administrative Operations. Manages centralized site work request function (work orders) including generation of routine PM actions, routing information for approval to necessary personnel (e.g. Maintenance Supervisors Engineer, Quality Control), and closeout including customer follow up, archiving, drawing updates, etc. Establishes operating procedures for use of the CMMS system and monitors procedures and results to ensure that all personnel adhere to the same routines, updating as conditions change. Assures all materials required to complete the job are incorporated in Maintenance action during PM development and work order issuance. Generate cost and manpower projection estimates for future work, to be used for budgeting purpose as well as past manpower expenditures to be used for expense allocations. Develop and routinely publish performance reports including but not limited to work order volume, turnaround, aging, customer satisfaction, etc. Maintains OSHA, DEEP, EPA, NFPA and all other Preventative Maintenance programs by carefully managing system access, levels of security, Management of Change and other programs relating to equipment maintenance and history. Ensure all safety requirements, permits, and protective equipment is incorporated in CMMS scheduled and non-schedule maintenance actions. Manages central tracking system for Safety related work requests in association with site EHS department. Develops and manages program for key requests and door hardware repairs (track through CMMS). You need: The position of Facilities Planning Manager requires a highly organized person, preferably with a bachelor’s degree and a minimum of four (4) years of building and equipment maintenance experience. Equivalent work experience may also be considered in lieu of a bachelor's degree. Prior experience with development of maintenance management systems ideally from ground up. Communication skills, both written and oral, are required to establish effective working relationships with various personnel levels (senior leadership through bargaining unit). Demonstrated technical writing skills are also required. In addition, working knowledge of computer systems and programs such as Excel and Word are required. Working knowledge of various regulatory agency requirements as they relate to maintenance including but not limited to OSHA, IBC, DEEP, EPA. Must be self-directed, able to work with a minimum of supervision. Must be able to develop strategies and implementation plans for maintenance program implementation. The position requires initiative and self-motivation to identify problems accurately and develop solutions using creativity and good judgment. Strong knowledge of current Maintenance Practices and Procedures. Be able to resolve conflicts between system operating schedules and maintenance demands ensuring equipment and facilities are adequately maintained with a minimum of system/equipment downtime or impact on operations. Negotiating skills are required to bring consensus and compromise between various operating groups in developing PM standards, routines and schedules. Must have prior proven experience working with business office operations including procurement, accounting, invoice management, budget management and staff supervision in technical office environment. Must possess excellent interpersonal and written skills. Ability to work with individuals of all levels from a variety of backgrounds and interests. Computer and web-based skills required. What's in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment."
    }
  },
